00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
former pope benedict xvi failed to take  action against clerics in four cases of  alleged sexual abuse in his native  germany that's the conclusion of a  report by a munich law firm the  archdiocese of munich and freising asked  it to investigate allegations of sexual  abuse between 1945 and 2019. pope  emeritus benedict formerly joseph  ratzinger archbishop of munich has  previously denied wrongdoing over the  cases  essentially he claims a lack of  knowledge of the facts and a lack of  relevance under canon law  in doing so he continues to claim  ignorance even when in our opinion it is  difficult to reconcile this with the  facts of the case  the report says there were at least 497  victims of abuse mainly young males it  accuses cardinal reinhard marx the  current archbishop of munich of  misconduct in two suspected abuse cases  last year pope francis rejected an offer  by him to resign but the new claims have  brought fresh pain for survivors of  abuse in southern germany  clearly it affects me very much on an  emotional level and it's the same area  where the abuse also happened in my  childhood about two hours by train from  munich in a small town and of course  that revives some things from me from  that time  the archdiocese is set to give a full  response to the report next week while  the vaticans put out a statement that  doesn't mention pope benedict saying  it'll evaluate the full report benedict  who's 94 has lived a secluded life in  the vatican since stepping down as  leader of the world's roman catholics in  2013 the first person to do so in 600  years the catholic church has been  damaged by a series of abuse scandals in  countries including australia chile  france ireland and the united states in  germany a study commissioned by the  german bishops conference in 2018  concluded more than 1600 clergymen had  committed some form of sexual abuse  against nearly 4 000 minors the real  number of victims is thought to be much  higher nadim baba al-jazeera
 

